    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Working closely with medically complex preterm infants and experiencing first-hand the stress and trauma their new parents go through changed Rehana A. Salam's career trajectory. From the early start of leading nursing care at the University Hospital's neonatal intensive care unit, NICU, she has come a long way, becoming an accomplished public health researcher, a task force member for the World Health Organization, WHO, an innovation facilitator and a mentor for women and child health researchers.",
